WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.397
A reusable view can sit in the middle of a larger dependency chain.

00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:06.857
Base tables feed the view.

00:00:06.857 --> 00:00:14.242
A report may then query that view directly, or a common table expression may use the view as its starting point.

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:18.220
A dashboard or application may depend on the final result.

00:00:19.096 --> 00:00:23.968
This means one change near the beginning can affect several downstream objects.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:31.186
Before making a breaking change, ask: what uses this view, and what assumptions do those users make about it?
